-- title:
--   Deligne–Serre: conjugate eigensystems in weight one
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a positive natural number, let $\varepsilon$ be a Dirichlet character modulo $N$ with values in $\mathbb{C}$, and let $f$ be a cusp form of weight $1$ on $\Gamma_1(N)$. Write $a_n =$ [`ModularFormClass.qCoeff`](def/FLTPrelim_Modularity.html#L19) $f\,n$, the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $f$ of period $1$. Assume $a_1 = 1$ and that for every prime $p$ with $p \nmid N$ and every natural number $n$ (including $n = 0$) one has $a_{pn} + \varepsilon(p)\,[p \mid n]\,a_{n/p} = a_p a_n$, where the bracket is $1$ if $p \mid n$ and the whole term is $0$ otherwise. Then there is a $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra $R \subseteq \mathbb{C}$ which is finite as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module, together with witnesses that $a_p \in R$ for every prime $p \nmid N$ and that $\varepsilon(x) \in R$ for every $x \in \mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z}$, such that for every ring homomorphism $\tau \colon R \to \mathbb{C}$ there exist a Dirichlet character $\varepsilon'$ modulo $N$ and a cusp form $g$ of weight $1$ on $\Gamma_1(N)$, with coefficients $b_n =$ [`ModularFormClass.qCoeff`](def/FLTPrelim_Modularity.html#L19) $g\,n$, satisfying: $\varepsilon'(x) = \tau(\varepsilon(x))$ for all $x \in \mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z}$; $b_1 = 1$; $b_p = \tau(a_p)$ for every prime $p \nmid N$; and $b_{pn} + \varepsilon'(p)\,[p \mid n]\,b_{n/p} = b_p b_n$ for every prime $p \nmid N$ and every natural number $n$.
--
--   This is Proposition 2.7 of Deligne–Serre, parts (2.7.3)–(2.7.4), specialised to weight one and phrased through the ring homomorphisms of the order generated by the eigenvalues $a_p$ ($p \nmid N$) and the values of $\varepsilon$: every $\tau$-conjugate of the eigensystem of $f$ is again the eigensystem of a normalised weight-one eigenform of the same level and conjugated nebentypus. It is used by [`DeligneSerre.exists_finset_qCoeff_mem_of_upperDensity_le_of_weightOne_hecke_eigen`](thm.html#DeligneSerre.exists_finset_qCoeff_mem_of_upperDensity_le_of_weightOne_hecke_eigen), on the route to attaching Galois representations to weight-one eigenforms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DeligneSerre_exists_subalgebra_qCoeff_mem_forall_ringHom_exists_qCoeff_eq_of_weightOne_hecke_eigen.lean

